   From: davidc@cs.uwa.edu.au (David Cake)

   Now just imagine retaining the modern system of nations, but with
   one crucial difference. Imagine that it was posible, if you held
   clear title to a piece of land, to transfer the sovereignty of that
   land to another nation, and then (if it was your home) declare
   yourself a citizen of that country. Then nations become far more
   like PPLs than they are now. It is likely that some nations
   undergoing particular economic disaster would then end up with
   virtually no citizens, and could then be 'taken over' by groups of
   new 'immigrants', and legally restructured. Is this the back door
   to PPL?

But no individual actually owns any land at present -- the nations do,
and individuals just own certain usage rights.  So you can't transfer
a piece of land out.  (And there is no reason that PPLs won't copy
this aspect of the present nation-states.)

Besides, (with the fall of "Communism") most nations that are
suffering economic disaster are perfectly willing to let people leave.
It is nations that are *not* suffering economic disaster that are
unwilling to let people enter!

